{
  // A faction (docs/story/STORY.md "Factions"): who they are, where they live, what is theirs, what they want, how they rate
  // the players, and the deeds they remember. A deed is an event of "verb" whose "theirs" role (the target unless named) is
  // the faction's: the faction itself, one of its members, or a construct it claims. The doer must be a player; the deed
  // adds 1 to the "remember" relation the faction holds towards them and their group, moves its standing with both by
  // "standing" (from -100 to 100), and its "wants" by theirs. Standing is the faction's Likes (above 0) or Grudge (below).
  // Its words are in Story/Office/IT.json, whose pages, replies and notices can ask about all of this ("when").
  // "teaches": technologies (parts an Assembler won't build until the faction has taught them), taught for good the first
  // time its standing with a player or group comes to the tier. "rivals": a rise in its standing takes that share (percent)
  // of the rise off the rival's. A deed with "whose" is against another faction's things (someone else's vans).
  "format": "call-of-slop-faction/1",
